m/standard/standard","homepage":"https://standardjs.com","size":3752,"stargazers_count":29401,"watchers_count":29401,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":false,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":2324,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":129,"license":{"key":"mit","name":"MIT License","spdx_id":"MIT","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/mit","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTEz"},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["development","ecmascript","es6","eslint","javascript","linter","nodejs","standard","static-code-analysis","style-guide"],"visibility":"public","forks":2324,"open_issues":129,"watchers":29401,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"The goal of this release is to make `standard` faster to install, and simpler to use.\n- [x] Remove `standard-format` (#340) (#397)\n  - Eliminates 250 packages, and cuts install time in half!\n  - For npm2, install went from 20 secs to 10 secs.\n  - For npm3, install went from 24 secs to 12 secs.\n- [x] Remove React rules (#351) (#367) (https://github.com/feross/eslint-config-standard-react/pull/13)\n  - JSX is still supported, but `standard` no longer assumes that JSX === React, so users can use alternatives like `virtual-dom` or `deku`.\n  - Rules come from `eslint-config-standard-jsx` instead of `eslint-config-standard-react` now.\n- [x] Expose eslint configuration via command line options and `package.json` \"standard\" property\n  - [x] Set \"plugins\" (https://github.com/feross/standard/issues/386)\n  - [x] Set \"rules\" (https://github.com/feross/standard/issues/367)\n  - [x] Set \"env\" (https://github.com/feross/standard/issues/371)\n- [x] Upgrade to ESLint v2 (stable release is imminent)\n  - There may be slight behavior changes to existing rules. When possible, we've noted these in the \"Rule changes\" section.\n- [x] Rule changes [% of standard users with new rule failures is noted in brackets]\n  - [x] New rule: Disallow `__dirname`/`__filename` string concatenation (#403) ([no-path-concat](http://eslint.org/docs/2.0.0/rules/no-path-concat)) [5%]\n  - [x] New rule: Require parens in arrow function arguments  (#309) ([arrow-parens](http://eslint.org/docs/2.0.0/rules/arrow-parens.html)) [5%]\n  - [x] New rule: Ensure that `new Promise()` is instantiated with the parameter names\n    `resolve`, `reject` (#282) ([promise/param-names](https://github.com/xjamundx/eslint-plugin-promise#param-names)) [1%]\n  - [x] New rule: Enforce Usage of Spacing in Template Strings ([template-curly-spacing](http://eslint.org/docs/2.0.0/rules/template-curly-spacing)) [1%]\n  - [x] New rule: Template strings are only allowed when necessary, i.e. template string features are being used (eslint got stricter: https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/5147) [1%]\n  - [x] New rule: Better dead code detection after conditional statements (eslint got stricter) [1%]\n  - [x] New rule: Enforce spaces around `*` in `yield * something` (#335) ([yield-star-spacing](http://eslint.org/docs/2.0.0/rules/yield-star-spacing)) [0%]\n  - [x] New rule: Disallow labels on loops/switch statements too (made rule stricter) ([no-labels](http://eslint.org/docs/2.0.0/rules/no-labels.html)) [0%]\n  - [x] New rule: Disallow unnecessary constructor ([no-useless-constructor](http://eslint.org/docs/2.0.0/rules/no-useless-constructor)) [0%]\n  - [x] New rule: Disallow empty destructuring patterns ([no-empty-pattern](http://eslint.org/docs/2.0.0/rules/no-empty-pattern)) [0%]\n  - [x] New rule: Disallow Symbol Constructor ([no-new-symbol](http://eslint.org/docs/2.0.0/rules/no-new-symbol)) [0%]\n  - [x] New rule: Disallow Self Assignment ([no-self-assign](http://eslint.org/docs/2.0.0/rules/no-self-assign)) [0%]\n  - [x] Relax rule: `parseInt()` radix rule because ES5 fixes this issue (#384)  ([radix](ht